  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 259 PM CDT Thu Oct 1 2026\n\nThe cold front and accompanying rainfall will have mostly cleared \nthe area by Friday afternoon, and we'll notice the difference. High \ntemperatures are forecast in the 60s areawide - a 10 to 20 degree \ndrop from today - and lows will fall into the 40s and 50s Friday \nnight. These lows will stick around for the next week, so dust off \nyour jacket if you haven't already. You won't need the jacket by \nafternoon, though, as highs are expected to climb into the 70s each \nday. A secondary cold front moving through the region early next \nweek will help keep things in check as well as scour out any \nlingering moisture from the region. In short, next week will be \ncooler, dry, and perfect for outdoor activities.",
